{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Offer: the cart's one upsell card per product family.

  By request (2026-09-11): "there should always be upsells in the cart even if
  they order max orbs or max game boys -- game boys add another case option,
  orbs add more orbs -- less cluttered, cleaner, simpler; they should still
  be able to choose Pokemons and GBs; optimised for iPhone 16 Pro Max and
  iPhone 13."

  WHAT IT REPLACES. Four writers each put their own row into #pg-unlock-slot:
  pg-unlock (the Buy-2-Get-1 rails, with a chooser that opens under the row),
  pg-cart-tune (the Duo Pack upgrade and the stand-alone spare case),
  pg-frame-add (the case / frame accessory). A one-console cart showed two or
  three of them stacked, and every one of them went quiet at the top of its
  ladder -- three Trio Packs, nine orbs -- leaving nothing to offer. Those rows
  are hidden here (display:none; their scripts keep running unchanged, and one
  of them, pg-unlock, also carries the drawer's duplicate-line repair, which
  must not be switched off), and this section paints the offers instead.

  ONE CARD, for the product the shopper added LAST (by request, 2026-09-11:
  "limit it to 1 upsell max; it should go off the product they added, but if
  they max out that product with all item combos then move to the next
  item"). /cart.js lists lines newest first, so the first line whose handle
  is known names the family (the free case counts as the console's). That
  family's deal is offered; when it has none left -- every console has a case,
  or the orbs are past the ladder with no free unit to promise -- the other
  families in the cart are tried, newest first; only when no family has a
  deal is a plain "add another" (or, with no orbs held, a Crystal Legends Orb)
  offered, so the cart is never without a card. The deals, per family:

    consoles   1 single ............ Add a 2nd: the Duo Pack (GB picker)
               2 singles ........... Switch to the Duo Pack (same consoles, less)
               Duo Pack ............ Add a 3rd: the Trio Pack (GB picker)
               3 singles ........... Switch to the Trio Pack
               anything else ....... one card for the cases still missing
                                     (the free gift is one per order, so a
                                     Trio wants two); then the family is done
    orbs       the next rung of the ladder the product page sells --
               Buy 2 Get 1 (repeats), Buy 5 Get 4 (once) -- phrased as the
               shopper experiences it: "Add 2 more, get 1 FREE", "Add your
               FREE 3rd Orb"; one design picker per orb added, defaulted to
               designs not already in the cart. Past the ladder's top the
               repeating Buy 2 Get 1 is offered again once it beats the
               Buy 5 Get 4 already earned (from 12 orbs); between 9 and 11
               no free-orb promise is honest, so the family is done and the
               single orb it can still offer is the plain fallback.
    wall art   the repeating Buy 2 Get 1, the same way.

  THE MATHS IS THE DISCOUNTS'. Read from the admin on 2026-09-11:
  "PokeOrb - Buy 2 Get 1 Free" ACTIVE, unlimited per order; "PokeOrb - Buy 5
  Get 4 Free" ACTIVE, once per order; "Wall Art - Buy 2 Get 1 Free" ACTIVE,
  unlimited; "Extra 10% off entire order" ACTIVE. The packs are products with
  their own prices and compare-at prices, read live from /products/*.js so an
  admin reprice propagates on its own. The SAVE chip measures what the row
  prints: free units against units x price, a pack against its compare-at,
  and a plain single against the product's compare-at -- the same measure the
  product page tiles and the cart lines use.

  HOW IT ADDS. Orbs and prints: one line per chosen design (a mixed three
  still earns the free one -- different variants of one product all qualify).
  Pack upgrades: the single line is taken out BY LINE KEY and the pack variant
  that holds those consoles plus the picked one goes in, so the cart charges
  exactly the pack price the row printed. Every write is checked for r.ok and
  the second write never follows a failed first one. The drawer is then
  refreshed through pg-drawer's own pgDrawerRefresh.

  HOW IT WATCHES. /cart.js is shared with half a dozen sections and throttled
  under their load, so this reads on the drawer's pg:cart-updated event and a
  debounced observer, plus a slow 4s beat, single-flight with a watchdog. A
  changed cart must be seen on two consecutive reads before the card is
  rebuilt (a read caught between two writes must never flash a wrong offer);
  our own add forces the rebuild. An unchanged cart is a no-op, so an open
  picker is never yanked mid-choice.

  THE SLOT is pg-unlock's #pg-unlock-slot, created here if it is not there
  yet, in the same position (above the item list) so pg-cart-mobile's
  placeUnlock() and pg-unlock agree with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the rows this card replaces; their scripts keep running unchanged */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-unlock,
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-soloff,
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-duoup,
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-frameoffer{display:none !important}

  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer{
    display:grid !important;
    grid-template-columns:48px minmax(0,1fr);
    grid-auto-flow:row;
    column-gap:10px;row-gap:7px;align-items:center;
    margin:6px 0 6px;padding:9px 10px 10px;
    border:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.3);border-radius:14px;
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#F8F3FC,#F1E7F8);
    box-shadow:0 12px 30px -24px rgba(74,28,102,.45);
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
    box-sizing:border-box;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer > img{
    grid-column:1;width:44px !important;min-width:44px !important;height:44px !important;
    flex:none;border-radius:11px !important;object-fit:cover !important;background:#efe4f8;display:block !important;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-t{grid-column:2;min-width:0}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-t b{
    display:block;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.25;color:#3B1553;font-weight:800;
    white-space:normal;overflow-wrap:anywhere;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-px{
    display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:2px 7px;
    margin-top:2px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:800;color:#7A2FA2;line-height:1.3;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-px s{color:#666;font-weight:400;font-size:12.5px;white-space:nowrap}   /* #666, not #8a8a8a: "more visible", by request */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-sv{
    display:inline-block;padding:3px 7px;border-radius:999px;
    font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:normal;text-transform:uppercase;font-style:normal;
    /* still, by request: the card's SAVE chip does not move (the cart lines' chips do) */
    color:#fff;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4,#7A2FA2);animation:none;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-t small{display:block;font-size:11px;line-height:1.3;color:#6E5C80;margin-top:2px}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-t small.pg-offer-inc{color:#7A2FA2;font-weight:600}

  /* the pickers: one per unit, in a row that wraps; the free ones say so */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-picks{grid-column:1 / -1;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px;min-width:0}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-picks:empty{display:none}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick{
    flex:1 1 calc(33.333% - 4px);max-width:100%;
    display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;min-width:0;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick span{
    font-size:9.5px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A2FA2;padding-left:2px;
  }
  /* the free ones pop: hot pink on the lavender card, by request */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick span.is-free{color:#E6007E}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick select{
    -webkit-appearance:none;-moz-appearance:none;appearance:none;
    width:100% !important;max-width:100% !important;min-width:0 !important;box-sizing:border-box !important;
    height:30px !important;min-height:0 !important;padding:0 24px 0 8px !important;margin:0 !important;
    border:1.5px solid rgba(122,47,162,.35) !important;border-radius:9px !important;
    background:#fff url("data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='11' height='7' viewBox='0 0 11 7'%3E%3Cpath d='M1 1l4.5 4.5L10 1' fill='none' stroke='%237A2FA2' stroke-width='1.8' stroke-linecap='round'/%3E%3C/svg%3E") no-repeat right 9px center !important;
    color:#3B1553 !important;font-family:inherit !important;font-size:12px !important;font-weight:700 !important;
    line-height:28px !important;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:none !important;
  }
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick select:focus{outline:2px solid #9B4BC4;outline-offset:1px}

  /* the one button: full width, the site's moving purple at the same 8s */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-add{
    grid-column:1 / -1;display:flex !important;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;
    width:100% !important;min-width:0 !important;max-width:none !important;margin:0 !important;
    min-height:38px !important;padding:0 12px !important;
    border:0 !important;border-radius:11px !important;
    background-color:#7A2FA2 !important;
    background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 30%,#4A1C66 50%,#7A2FA2 70%,#9B4BC4 100%) !important;
    background-size:240% 240% !important;animation:pgWave 8s ease-in-out infinite !important;
    color:#fff !important;-webkit-text-fill-color:#fff !important;
    font-family:inherit !important;font-size:12.5px !important;font-weight:800 !important;
    letter-spacing:.06em !important;text-transform:uppercase !important;line-height:1 !important;
    box-shadow:0 12px 26px -12px rgba(139,68,190,.7) !important;cursor:pointer;
    transition:filter .15s ease,opacity .15s ease;
  }
  html body #cart .pg-offer-add::before,html body #cart .pg-offer-add::after{display:none !important;content:none !important;background:none !important}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-add:after{display:none}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-add:hover{filter:brightness(1.08)}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-add[disabled]{opacity:.65 !important;cursor:default}
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-add .arr{font-size:16px;line-height:1}

  /* iPhone 13 (390) and the compact block pg-cart-timer stamps under 414px:
     a touch tighter, and never narrower than the 34px touch height */
  @media (max-width:414px){
    #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer{padding:8px 9px 9px;column-gap:9px;row-gap:6px}
    #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-t b{font-size:13px}
    #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-px{font-size:13px}
    #cart#cart#cart#cart .pg-offer-pick{flex-basis:calc(33.333% - 4px)}
  }
  /* the pinned pane, if a stale pg-cart-mobile ever seats the slot there */
  #cart#cart#cart#cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-offer{margin:0 0 6px}
  @keyframes pgWave{0%{background-position:0% 50%}50%{background-position:100% 50%}100%{background-position:0% 50%}}
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgCartOffer) return; window.pgCartOffer = 1;

  var H = {
    orb:   'pokemon-crystal-ball-3d-pikachu-gengar-mewtwo-night-light-lamp-pokeball-3d-glass-pokemon-crystal-ball-statue-kids-birthday-gift',
    wall:  'anime-pokemon-3d-lenticular-poster-charizard-squirtle-bulbasaur-come-alive-with-amazing-3d-effects-wall-art-printwithout-frame',
    con:   'handheld-game-console',
    duo:   'r36s-duo-pack',
    trio:  'r36s-trio-pack',
    kase:  'r36s-protective-case-free-gift'
  };
  var SPARE_CASE = 49640879063268;           /* $13.99 "Spare case" */
  var FREE_CASE  = 49640846426340;           /* $0.00 "Free with console" */
  var SIZE_OF = {49622431858916: '64', 49622431826148: '128'};   /* console variant -> GB */
  var CASE_IMG = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0815/5706/1860/files/hf_20260810_234744_eb2ec102-427d-4c23-94f0-453e70014817.png?v=1786422962&width=120';

  function money(c){ return '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2); }
  function pct(was, now){ return was > now ? Math.floor((was - now) / was * 100) : 0; }

  /* THE EXTRA 10% IS IN THE PRICE. The admin's "Extra 10% off entire order"
     (automatic, every item, stacks with the Buy X Get Y) comes off at checkout,
     so a card that printed the catalogue price overstated what the shopper
     would pay; by request (2026-09-11) every card prints the net figure and
     says so on a line of its own ("Extra 10% off included"). The rate is READ FROM THE CART, not
     hard-coded: Shopify allocates that discount onto every paid line
     (line_level_discount_allocations, an automatic percentage over all
     items), so switching it off in the admin drops it out of these prices on
     the next read. A cart with no paid line to read falls back to the
     admin's 10%. The Buy X Get Y allocations are percentage discounts too, but
     over the entitled item only, and are not counted. */
  var RATE = 0.10;
  function readRate(cart){
    var found = null;
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      if (found !== null || !it.line_price) return;
      var r = 0;
      (it.line_level_discount_allocations || []).forEach(function(a){
        var d = a && a.discount_application;
        if (d && d.type === 'automatic' && d.value_type === 'percentage' && d.target_type === 'line_item' && d.target_selection === 'all') r = Math.max(r, parseFloat(d.value || 0) / 100);
      });
      found = r;
    });
    return found === null ? 0.10 : Math.min(found, 0.9);
  }
  function net(c){ return Math.round(c * (1 - RATE)); }
  /* a line's price before any discount (the compare-at figures the cards are
     measured against are gross too); older carts only carry line_price */
  function gross(it){ return it.original_line_price != null ? it.original_line_price : it.line_price; }
  function ord(k){ var t = k % 10, h = k % 100; return k + (t === 1 && h !== 11 ? 'st' : t === 2 && h !== 12 ? 'nd' : t === 3 && h !== 13 ? 'rd' : 'th'); }
  function nths(from, to){ var p = []; for (var i = from; i <= to; i++) p.push(ord(i)); var l = p.pop(); return (p.length ? p.join(', ') + ' & ' : '') + l; }
  function thumb(src){ return src ? String(src).replace(/(\.[a-z]+)(\?|$)/i, '_120x$1$2') : ''; }
  function esc(s){ return String(s).replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/"/g, '&quot;'); }

  /* ---------------- products, read once ---------------- */
  var P = {}, PBUSY = {};
  function product(handle){
    if (P[handle]) return Promise.resolve(P[handle]);
    if (PBUSY[handle]) return PBUSY[handle];
    PBUSY[handle] = fetch('/products/' + handle + '.js').then(function(r){ return r.json(); }).then(function(pr){
      var out = {handle: handle, image: (pr.featured_image || (pr.images && pr.images[0]) || ''), variants: []};
      (pr.variants || []).forEach(function(v){
        out.variants.push({id: v.id, title: v.title, price: v.price, cap: v.compare_at_price || 0, available: v.available !== false,
          img: (v.featured_image && v.featured_image.src) || ''});
      });
      P[handle] = out; PBUSY[handle] = null; return out;
    }).catch(function(){ PBUSY[handle] = null; return null; });
    return PBUSY[handle];
  }
  /* a pack variant by the sorted GB sizes it holds ("64GB + 128GB") */
  function packBySizes(pr, sizes){
    var key = sizes.slice().sort(function(a, b){ return a - b; }).join('|');
    for (var i = 0; i < pr.variants.length; i++){
      var m = String(pr.variants[i].title).match(/\d+(?=GB)/g);
      if (m && m.slice().sort(function(a, b){ return a - b; }).join('|') === key && pr.variants[i].available) return pr.variants[i];
    }
    return null;
  }
  function sizesOfPack(title){ return (String(title).match(/\d+(?=GB)/g) || []); }

  /* ---------------- reading the cart ---------------- */
  function tally(cart){
    var t = {con: [], duo: [], trio: [], orb: [], wall: [], spares: 0, freeCase: 0, held: {}};
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      var h = it.handle || '';
      if (h === H.con) t.con.push(it);
      else if (h === H.duo) t.duo.push(it);
      else if (h === H.trio) t.trio.push(it);
      else if (h === H.orb) t.orb.push(it);
      else if (h === H.wall) t.wall.push(it);
      else if (h === H.kase){ if (it.variant_id === SPARE_CASE) t.spares += it.quantity; else t.freeCase += it.quantity; }
      (t.held[h] = t.held[h] || {})[it.variant_id] = true;
    });
    t.conUnits = 0; t.con.forEach(function(it){ t.conUnits += it.quantity; });
    t.duoUnits = 0; t.duo.forEach(function(it){ t.duoUnits += it.quantity; });
    t.trioUnits = 0; t.trio.forEach(function(it){ t.trioUnits += it.quantity; });
    t.consoles = t.conUnits + 2 * t.duoUnits + 3 * t.trioUnits;
    t.orbUnits = 0; t.orb.forEach(function(it){ t.orbUnits += it.quantity; });
    t.wallUnits = 0; t.wall.forEach(function(it){ t.wallUnits += it.quantity; });
    return t;
  }

  /* the console family's one offer */
  function consoleOffer(t){
    if (!t.consoles) return Promise.resolve(null);
    var single = t.con[0];
    /* 1 or 2 or 3 loose singles, no pack: the pack that holds exactly them (plus one picked) */
    if (!t.duoUnits && !t.trioUnits && t.conUnits >= 1 && t.conUnits <= 3){
      var sizes = [];
      t.con.forEach(function(it){ for (var i = 0; i < it.quantity; i++) sizes.push(SIZE_OF[it.variant_id] || '64'); });
      if (t.conUnits === 1){
        var handle = H.duo;
        return Promise.all([product(H.con), product(handle)]).then(function(r){
          var con = r[0], pack = r[1]; if (!con || !pack) return null;
          var isDuo = true;
          var pickDefault = sizes[sizes.length - 1];
          var withPick = packBySizes(pack, sizes.concat([pickDefault])); if (!withPick) return null;
          return {
            kind: 'pack', key: 'pack:' + handle + ':' + sizes.join('|'),
            handle: handle, packSizes: sizes, lines: t.con,
            img: thumb(con.image),
            title: isDuo ? 'Add a 2nd R36S: the Duo Pack' : 'Add a 3rd R36S: the Trio Pack',
            sub: isDuo ? 'Two consoles, one price' : 'Three consoles, one price',   /* no "+$" figure here, by request */
            was: withPick.cap || withPick.price, now: withPick.price,
            picks: [{label: 'GB for the new one', options: [{id: '64', t: '64GB'}, {id: '128', t: '128GB'}], value: pickDefault}],
            btn: 'Upgrade to the ' + (isDuo ? 'Duo' : 'Trio') + ' Pack',
            pack: pack
          };
        });
      }
      /* two or three loose singles: the pack holding exactly them, for less */
      var packH = t.conUnits === 2 ? H.duo : H.trio, packName = t.conUnits === 2 ? 'Duo' : 'Trio';
      return product(packH).then(function(pack){
        if (!pack) return null;
        var v = packBySizes(pack, sizes); if (!v) return null;
        var singlesNow = 0; t.con.forEach(function(it){ singlesNow += gross(it); });
        if (v.price >= singlesNow) return null;
        /* both sides carry the extra 10% at checkout, so the saving is net too */
        var less = net(singlesNow) - net(v.price);
        return {
          kind: 'switch', key: 'switch:' + packH + ':' + sizes.join('|'), handle: packH, variant: v, lines: t.con,
          img: thumb(v.img || pack.image),
          title: 'Switch to the ' + packName + ' Pack', sub: 'Same ' + (t.conUnits === 2 ? 'two' : 'three') + ' consoles, ' + money(less) + ' less',
          was: v.cap || singlesNow, now: v.price, picks: [], btn: 'Switch to the ' + packName + ' Pack — save ' + money(less)
        };
      });
    }
    /* a Duo Pack (and nothing else on the console side): the Trio holding it plus one */
    if (t.duoUnits === 1 && !t.trioUnits && !t.conUnits){
      return Promise.all([product(H.duo), product(H.trio)]).then(function(r){
        var duo = r[0], trio = r[1]; if (!duo || !trio) return null;
        var line = t.duo[0], sizes = sizesOfPack(line.title || line.product_title || '');
        duo.variants.forEach(function(v){ if (String(v.id) === String(line.variant_id)) sizes = sizesOfPack(v.title); });
        if (sizes.length !== 2) return null;
        var pickDefault = sizes[1];
        var withPick = packBySizes(trio, sizes.concat([pickDefault])); if (!withPick) return null;
        return {
          kind: 'pack', key: 'pack:' + H.trio + ':' + sizes.join('|'), handle: H.trio, packSizes: sizes, lines: t.duo,
          img: thumb(withPick.img || trio.image),
          title: 'Add a 3rd R36S: the Trio Pack',
          sub: 'Three consoles, one price',
          was: withPick.cap || withPick.price, now: withPick.price,
          picks: [{label: 'GB for the new one', options: [{id: '64', t: '64GB'}, {id: '128', t: '128GB'}], value: pickDefault}],
          btn: 'Upgrade to the Trio Pack', pack: trio
        };
      });
    }
    /* every other console cart: a case for every console that has none, in
       ONE card (the first case is the free gift, one per order, so a Trio is
       offered two cases, not one -- by request, 2026-09-11); then an orb */
    var needCases = t.consoles - 1 - t.spares;
    if (needCases > 0){
      return product(H.kase).then(function(pr){
        var v = null; (pr ? pr.variants : []).forEach(function(x){ if (x.id === SPARE_CASE) v = x; });
        var unit = (v && v.price) || 1399, cap = (v && v.cap) || 2499;
        return {
          kind: 'add', key: 'case:' + t.spares + ':' + needCases, items: [{id: SPARE_CASE, quantity: needCases}],
          img: thumb((v && v.img) || (pr && pr.image) || CASE_IMG),
          title: needCases > 1 ? 'Add ' + needCases + ' protective cases' : (t.spares ? 'Add another protective case' : 'Add a spare protective case'),
          sub: needCases > 1 ? 'One per console; the 1st is free' : (t.freeCase ? 'One case already comes free with your console' : 'Zip case, fitted for the R36S'),
          was: cap * needCases, now: unit * needCases, picks: [], btn: needCases > 1 ? 'Add ' + needCases + ' cases' : 'Add the case'
        };
      });
    }
    return Promise.resolve(null);   /* every console has a case: this family is done */
  }

  /* the orb (and wall art) ladder, phrased as the shopper experiences it */
  var RUNGS = {};
  RUNGS[H.orb]  = {name: 'Orb', rungs: [{paid: 2, free: 1}, {paid: 5, free: 4}], repeats: true, top: 4};
  RUNGS[H.wall] = {name: 'Print', rungs: [{paid: 2, free: 1}], repeats: true, top: 0};

  function ladderOffer(handle, units, lines, held, cross){
    var L = RUNGS[handle];
    return product(handle).then(function(pr){
      if (!pr) return null;
      var unitV = null;
      if (lines.length) pr.variants.forEach(function(v){ if (String(v.id) === String(lines[0].variant_id)) unitV = v; });
      var unit = unitV ? unitV.price : (pr.variants[0] ? pr.variants[0].price : 0);
      var cap = unitV ? unitV.cap : (pr.variants[0] ? pr.variants[0].cap : 0);
      if (!unit) return null;
      var n = units;
      if (cross && !n){
        var one = pr.variants.filter(function(v){ return v.available; }).map(function(v){ return {id: String(v.id), t: v.title, img: v.img}; });
        return {
          kind: 'add', key: 'cross:' + handle, handle: handle, need: 1, single: one.length < 2 ? one[0] : null, plain: true,
          img: thumb(pr.image), title: 'Add a Crystal Legends ' + L.name, sub: 'Buy 2, Get 1 FREE',
          was: cap || unit, now: unit, btn: 'Add to cart',
          picks: one.length > 1 ? [{label: L.name, free: false, options: one, value: one[0].id}] : []
        };
      }
      var freeNow = 0;
      L.rungs.forEach(function(g){ if (g.paid + g.free <= n && g.free > freeNow) freeNow = g.free; });
      if (L.repeats) freeNow = Math.max(freeNow, Math.floor(n / 3) * L.rungs[0].free);
      var paidNow = n - freeNow;
      var need = 0, paidAdded = 0, freeAdded = 0, tier = null;
      for (var i = 0; i < L.rungs.length; i++){
        var g = L.rungs[i];
        if (g.paid < paidNow) continue;
        if (g.paid + g.free <= n) continue;
        tier = g; need = g.paid + g.free - n; paidAdded = Math.max(0, g.paid - paidNow); freeAdded = Math.max(0, need - paidAdded); break;
      }
      if (!tier && L.repeats){
        /* past the ladder: the repeating Buy 2 Get 1, once it beats what is held */
        var m = 3 * (freeNow + 1);
        if (m - n <= 3){ tier = L.rungs[0]; need = m - n; freeAdded = 1; paidAdded = need - 1; }
      }
      var title, sub, was, now, btn, plain = false;
      if (tier && need > 0){
        if (paidAdded === 0){
          title = 'Add your FREE ' + nths(n + 1, n + need) + ' ' + L.name + (need > 1 ? 's' : '');
          sub = '';   /* the title already says it, by request */
        } else {
          title = 'Buy ' + paidAdded + ' more, get ' + freeAdded + ' FREE';
          sub = '';
        }
        was = unit * need; now = unit * paidAdded;
        btn = 'Add ' + need + ' to cart' + (freeAdded ? ' — ' + freeAdded + ' FREE' : '');
      } else {
        need = 1; paidAdded = 1; freeAdded = 0; plain = true;   /* no free unit to promise: the family is done */
        title = cross ? 'Add a Crystal Legends ' + L.name : 'Add another ' + L.name;
        sub = '';   /* the note under the cards names the extra 10% */
        was = cap || unit; now = unit; btn = 'Add to cart';
      }
      var opts = pr.variants.filter(function(v){ return v.available; }).map(function(v){ return {id: String(v.id), t: v.title, img: v.img}; });
      var heldHere = held[handle] || {};
      var fresh = opts.filter(function(o){ return !heldHere[o.id]; });
      var pool = fresh.length >= need ? fresh : opts;
      var picks = [];
      if (opts.length > 1){
        for (var k = 0; k < need; k++){
          var isFree = k >= need - freeAdded;
          picks.push({label: isFree ? 'Free' : L.name + ' ' + (k + 1), free: isFree, options: opts, value: pool[k % pool.length].id});
        }
      }
      return {
        kind: 'add', key: 'ladder:' + handle + ':' + n + ':' + need, handle: handle, need: need, single: opts.length < 2 ? opts[0] : null,
        img: thumb(pr.image), title: title, sub: sub, was: was, now: now, picks: picks, btn: btn, plain: plain
      };
    });
  }
  function orbOffer(t, cross){ return ladderOffer(H.orb, t.orbUnits, t.orb, t.held, !!cross); }

  /* the families in the cart, the one the shopper added last first. /cart.js
     lists lines newest first; a line of an unknown handle names no family */
  var FAMILY = {};
  FAMILY[H.con] = FAMILY[H.duo] = FAMILY[H.trio] = FAMILY[H.kase] = 'console';
  FAMILY[H.orb] = 'orb'; FAMILY[H.wall] = 'wall';
  function familiesByRecency(cart){
    var out = [];
    (cart.items || []).forEach(function(it){
      var f = FAMILY[it.handle || ''];
      if (f && out.indexOf(f) === -1) out.push(f);
    });
    return out;
  }
  function familyOffer(f, t){
    if (f === 'console') return consoleOffer(t);
    if (f === 'orb') return orbOffer(t, false);
    if (f === 'wall') return ladderOffer(H.wall, t.wallUnits, t.wall, t.held, false);
    return Promise.resolve(null);
  }
  function offersFor(cart){
    RATE = readRate(cart);
    var t = tally(cart);
    var fams = familiesByRecency(cart);
    if (!fams.length) return Promise.resolve([]);
    return Promise.all(fams.map(function(f){ return familyOffer(f, t); })).then(function(list){
      /* ONE CARD. The newest family's deal; failing that, the next family's;
         a plain "add another" only when no family has a deal left; and with no
         orbs held, a Crystal Legends Orb as the last resort. */
      var deal = null, plain = null;
      list.forEach(function(o){
        if (!o) return;
        if (!o.plain && !deal) deal = o;
        if (o.plain && !plain) plain = o;
      });
      if (deal) return [deal];
      if (plain) return [plain];
      if (!t.orbUnits) return orbOffer(t, true).then(function(o){ return o ? [o] : []; });
      return [];
    });
  }

  /* ---------------- the card ---------------- */
  function card(o){
    var el = document.createElement('div');
    el.className = 'pg-offer';
    el.setAttribute('data-offer', o.key);
    var picks = '';
    (o.picks || []).forEach(function(p, i){
      picks += '<label class="pg-offer-pick"><span' + (p.free ? ' class="is-free"' : '') + '>' + esc(p.label) + '</span><select data-i="' + i + '">';
      p.options.forEach(function(op){ picks += '<option value="' + esc(op.id) + '"' + (String(op.id) === String(p.value) ? ' selected' : '') + '>' + esc(op.t) + '</option>'; });
      picks += '</select></label>';
    });
    var now = o.now ? net(o.now) : 0;      /* what the till will take, extra 10% included */
    var save = pct(o.was, now);
    /* every card says so itself ("state it in the upsell", by request) */
    var inc = RATE > 0 ? 'Extra ' + Math.round(RATE * 100) + '% off included' : '';
    el.innerHTML =
      '<img alt="" width="48" height="48" decoding="sync" src="' + esc(o.img || '') + '">' +
      '<div class="pg-offer-t"><b>' + esc(o.title) + '</b>' +
        '<span class="pg-offer-px">' + (o.was > now ? '<s>' + money(o.was) + '</s>' : '') + (now === 0 ? 'FREE' : money(now)) +
          (save ? '<i class="pg-offer-sv">Save ' + save + '%</i>' : '') + '</span>' +
        (o.sub ? '<small>' + esc(o.sub) + '</small>' : '') +
        (inc ? '<small class="pg-offer-inc">' + inc + '</small>' : '') + '</div>' +
      '<div class="pg-offer-picks">' + picks + '</div>' +
      '<button type="button" class="pg-offer-add">' + esc(o.btn) + '<span class="arr">→</span></button>';
    el.pgOffer = o;
    return el;
  }

  function slotFor(c){
    var list = c.querySelector('.l4ca:not(.in-panel)');
    if (!list) return null;
    var slot = c.querySelector('#pg-unlock-slot');
    if (!slot){
      slot = document.createElement('div');
      slot.id = 'pg-unlock-slot';
      list.parentNode.insertBefore(slot, list);
    }
    return slot;
  }

  function paint(offers){
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c) return;
    var slot = slotFor(c);
    if (!slot) return;
    var want = {};
    offers.forEach(function(o){ want[o.key] = o; });
    slot.querySelectorAll('.pg-offer').forEach(function(el){
      var k = el.getAttribute('data-offer');
      if (!want[k]){ el.parentNode.removeChild(el); return; }
      want[k].el = el;   /* same offer: keep it, and whatever the shopper picked */
    });
    var prev = null;
    offers.forEach(function(o, i){
      var el = o.el || card(o);
      el.style.order = String(-10 + i);   /* ahead of the hidden rows */
      if (!o.el){
        if (prev && prev.nextSibling) slot.insertBefore(el, prev.nextSibling);
        else if (prev) slot.appendChild(el);
        else slot.insertBefore(el, slot.firstChild);
      }
      prev = el;
    });
    if (window.pgPlaceUnlock){ try { window.pgPlaceUnlock(); } catch(e){} }
  }

  /* ---------------- watching ---------------- */
  var busy = false, watch = null, lastSig = null, seenSig = null, force = false;
  function sig(cart){ return (cart.items || []).map(function(it){ return it.variant_id + 'x' + it.quantity; }).join(','); }
  function read(){
    if (busy){ return; }
    var c = document.getElementById('cart');
    if (!c || !c.querySelector('.l4ca:not(.in-panel)')) return;
    busy = true;
    clearTimeout(watch);
    watch = setTimeout(function(){ busy = false; }, 8000);
    fetch('/cart.js', {headers: {'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest'}}).then(function(r){ return r.json(); }).then(function(cart){
      var s = sig(cart);
      if (s === lastSig && document.querySelector('#cart .pg-offer, #cart #pg-unlock-slot')){
        /* unchanged: only make sure the cards are still standing (a drawer
           rebuild replaces #cart's innerHTML wholesale) */
        if (!document.querySelector('#cart .pg-offer') && lastOffers && lastOffers.length) paint(lastOffers);
        return;
      }
      if (!force && lastSig !== null && s !== seenSig){ seenSig = s; setTimeout(read, 600); return; }   /* a change is seen once, then confirmed */
      force = false; seenSig = s;
      return offersFor(cart).then(function(offers){ lastSig = s; lastOffers = offers; paint(offers); });
    }).catch(function(){}).then(function(){ clearTimeout(watch); busy = false; });
  }
  var lastOffers = null;
  var q = null;
  function schedule(ms){ if (q) return; q = setTimeout(function(){ q = null; read(); }, ms || 150); }

  /* ---------------- adding ---------------- */
  var adding = false;
  function post(url, body){
    return fetch(url, {method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}, credentials: 'same-origin', body: JSON.stringify(body)})
      .then(function(r){ if (!r || !r.ok) throw new Error('write ' + (r && r.status)); return r; });
  }
  function perform(o, el){
    var sels = el.querySelectorAll('.pg-offer-pick select');
    if (o.kind === 'add'){
      var items = [];
      if (o.items) items = o.items;
      else if (o.single) items = [{id: parseInt(o.single.id, 10), quantity: o.need}];
      else sels.forEach(function(s){ var id = parseInt(s.value, 10); if (id) items.push({id: id, quantity: 1}); });
      if (!items.length) return Promise.reject(new Error('nothing to add'));
      return post('/cart/add.js', {items: items});
    }
    if (o.kind === 'pack'){
      var size = sels[0] ? sels[0].value : '64';
      var v = packBySizes(o.pack, o.packSizes.concat([size]));
      if (!v) return Promise.reject(new Error('no pack variant'));
      /* out with the lines by KEY, then in with the pack; a failed removal never proceeds */
      var chain = Promise.resolve();
      o.lines.forEach(function(it){ chain = chain.then(function(){ return post('/cart/change.js', {id: it.key, quantity: 0}); }); });
      return chain.then(function(){ return post('/cart/add.js', {items: [{id: v.id, quantity: 1}]}); });
    }
    if (o.kind === 'switch'){
      var ch = Promise.resolve();
      o.lines.forEach(function(it){ ch = ch.then(function(){ return post('/cart/change.js', {id: it.key, quantity: 0}); }); });
      return ch.then(function(){ return post('/cart/add.js', {items: [{id: o.variant.id, quantity: 1}]}); });
    }
    return Promise.reject(new Error('unknown offer'));
  }
  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (!e.target || !e.target.closest) return;
    var btn = e.target.closest('#cart .pg-offer-add');
    if (!btn) return;
    e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation();
    if (e.stopImmediatePropagation) e.stopImmediatePropagation();
    if (adding) return;
    var el = btn.closest('.pg-offer'), o = el && el.pgOffer;
    if (!o) return;
    adding = true;
    var label = btn.innerHTML;
    btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Adding…';
    perform(o, el).then(function(){
      adding = false; force = true; lastSig = null;
      if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
      if (window.pgDrawerRefresh){ try { Promise.resolve(window.pgDrawerRefresh()).then(function(){ schedule(50); }, function(){ schedule(50); }); } catch(x){ schedule(50); } }
      else schedule(50);
      setTimeout(read, 1500);
    }).catch(function(){
      adding = false;
      btn.disabled = false; btn.innerHTML = label;
      btn.textContent = 'Try again';
    });
  }, true);
  /* a tap inside the card must not fall through to the theme's drawer handlers */
  document.addEventListener('click', function(e){
    if (e.target && e.target.closest && e.target.closest('#cart .pg-offer-pick')) e.stopPropagation();
  }, true);

  function boot(){
    read();
    document.addEventListener('pg:cart-updated', function(){ schedule(120); });
    if (window.MutationObserver){
      var mo = null;
      var hook = function(){
        var c = document.getElementById('cart');
        if (!c || c.pgOfferObs) return;
        c.pgOfferObs = 1;
        new MutationObserver(function(){ schedule(150); }).observe(c, {childList: true, subtree: true});
      };
      hook();
      mo = new MutationObserver(hook);
      mo.observe(document.documentElement, {childList: true, subtree: true});
    }
    setInterval(read, 4000);
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot); else boot();
})();
</script>
